{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition","id":1300213,"title":"Who Made Humans? [Any Edition]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-27T00:45:52-07:00","id":1300213,"title":"Who Made Humans? [Any Edition]","content":"Hello. I was wondering if it is ever stated in any of the editions which Primordial or Primordials made humans. If not, who would you personally guess it to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T02:10:53-07:00","id":1300219,"title":"","content":"I think it was second edition where they said the Primordials made humans to be a source of essence, since they were the weakest of the races so they basically spent their time fearfully praying for help and getting pushed around/sacrificed by the Dragon Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T02:14:14-07:00","id":1300220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300219#post1300219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was second edition where they said the Primordials made humans to be a source of essence, since they were the weakest of the races so they basically spent their time fearfully praying for help and getting pushed around/sacrificed by the Dragon Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I was asking which Primordial or Primordials made them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T02:28:26-07:00","id":1300221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300220#post1300220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but I was asking which Primordial or Primordials made them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errrr, all of them. They're having a party; Sacheverell is passed out on the couch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:08:02-07:00","id":1300223,"title":"","content":"Blame it on Autochthon. \u2026 somewhat.<br /> <br /> According to Scroll of Fallen Races, the Mountain Folk were first carved by Autochthon from a deposit of Jade in which fair folk were calcified when Gaia and Cytheria forged Creation from principles of Chaos and Order. Later these Jadeborn were used as the prototype for humanity when the Primordials sought a source of prayer.<br /> <br /> Although there is no explicit indication that the task was assigned to Autochthon, or if it was a group project. While Autochthon earned the moniker of the Great Maker, he's clearly not the only Primordial to ever create things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:24:27-07:00","id":1300225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300223#post1300223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame it on Autochthon. \u2026 somewhat.<br /> <br /> According to Scroll of Fallen Races, the Mountain Folk were first carved by Autochthon from a deposit of Jade in which fair folk were calcified when Gaia and Cytheria forged Creation from principles of Chaos and Order. Later these Jadeborn were used as the prototype for humanity when the Primordials sought a source of prayer.<br /> <br /> Although there is no explicit indication that the task was assigned to Autochthon, or if it was a group project. While Autochthon earned the moniker of the Great Maker, he's clearly not the only Primordial to ever create things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good. That makes it much easier for me to insert a custom Primordial as the creator of humanity, without having to switch things up too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:42:48-07:00","id":1300227,"title":"","content":"Actually, it wasn't copying the Jadeborn. The Primordials found Clayman, the prototype for the jadeborn, and dissected him in a way. Humanity was based on what they learned.<br /> <br /> So humanity was based on a fae to some degree. But seemed to be a group project","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T04:52:35-07:00","id":1300231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300225#post1300225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, good. That makes it much easier for me to insert a custom Primordial as the creator of humanity, without having to switch things up too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why attribute it to just one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T04:58:39-07:00","id":1300233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300231#post1300231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why attribute it to just one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm planning on having her be an ally to the characters, and the easiest way I can think of to both have her care about them and to have them be able to relate to her is to have it so she created humans and based their minds and personalities on herself, thus providing a reason to care (she cares about her creations) and making her more sympathetic (since she based human minds off of her own, she is the most easily understood Primordial and the most human-like in mindset, and so is easier to empathize with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 03-27-2019, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:50:36-07:00","id":1300248,"title":"","content":"Why not attribute it to Gaia then? She already has the Great Mother role all sewn up. Although she's also the Primordial embodiment of cyclones and volcanic cataclysms, which are a bit inhuman in their outlook. She's a complicated gal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:58:51-07:00","id":1300250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300248#post1300248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not attribute it to Gaia then? She already has the Great Mother role all sewn up. Although she's also the Primordial embodiment of cyclones and volcanic cataclysms, which are a bit inhuman in their outlook. She's a complicated gal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause she's not around much, and the Primordial was convinced by the Ebon Dragon to fight on behalf of the Primordials (which she now regrets), and is currently a Yozi. This means she can be summoned as a demon.<br /> <br /> Plus, I've already come up with a semi-large backstory including interactions with Autochthon and Sol and the creation of an Infernal Exalted, a personality, and am currently working on custom Infernal Charms, so...it would be kind of a waste to not use her now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 03-27-2019, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:03:18-07:00","id":1300254,"title":"","content":"she is not, she sided with the Gods. She's not one of the Yozi. As for what she represents, the Five Elements that make up Creation for one thing. Thst's her major contribution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:07:27-07:00","id":1300255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300254#post1300254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she is not, she sided with the Gods. She's not one of the Yozi. As for what she represents, the Five Elements that make up Creation for one thing. Thst's her major contribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I was saying my custom Primordial is currently a Yozi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:08:26-07:00","id":1300257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300254#post1300254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she is not, she sided with the Gods. She's not one of the Yozi. As for what she represents, the Five Elements that make up Creation for one thing. Thst's her major contribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ender means their Yozi when he uses 'she', not Gaia in that second sentence. She's not around much is valid for Gaia, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>