r\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300250#post1300250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> is currently a Yozi. This means she can be summoned as a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoahh, errrr... not usually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T07:26:52-07:00","id":1300275,"title":"","content":"Maybe with some sort of super-ritual? It's thematically possible I think (in 2nd ed, I think the Unconquered Sun could summon Yozi?), even if there are no rules for it.<br /> Not to say that you can do it canonically, there's no canonical way, but if the ST sets up some ancient and massive McGuffin ritual, I don't think it breaks the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, I thought that Autocthon made the prototype and then the other Primordials based humans on it... in a way that pissed him off?<br /> <br /> Certainly, I don't remember it being clear-cut enough that making a Primordial &quot;creator of humanity&quot; is utterly canon-breaking, if that's what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T07:29:25-07:00","id":1300277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300275#post1300275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe with some sort of super-ritual? It's thematically possible I think (in 2nd ed, I think the Unconquered Sun could summon Yozi?), even if there are no rules for it.<br /> Not to say that you can do it canonically, there's no canonical way, but if the ST sets up some ancient and massive McGuffin ritual, I don't think it breaks the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, I thought that Autocthon made the prototype and then the other Primordials based humans on it... in a way that pissed him off?<br /> <br /> Certainly, I don't remember it being clear-cut enough that making a Primordial &amp;quot;creator of humanity&amp;quot; is utterly canon-breaking, if that's what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The only way to get a yozi out was to be the unconquered sun or I believe saturn. There is no canon way for that to happen otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:00:12-07:00","id":1300349,"title":"","content":"Idea for 3e: humans were an accident. They lack the inherent supernatural powers of other sapient species because those species were created whole-form by Primordials while humans were shaped over eons in the Time Before by base animals mutating and being naturally selected by their environment. This is why humans were not Geased - they weren't created by the Primordials (save in that their equally non-magical base animal ancestors were if you go far back enough). As it was Gaia who designed the process of natural selection for said base animals, she takes credit as the &quot;midwife&quot; who facilitated humanity's delivery into the world, though not literal creator.<br /> <br /> This would of course be mutually exclusive with the &quot;humanity is a debased mockery of the Jadeborn template&quot; background, but I don't think that's a big loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:11:50-07:00","id":1300378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300263#post1300263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoahh, errrr... not usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to summoning her Fetich Soul. Due to some rather strange aspects of her existence, she is much closer to her souls than the other Yozi, and can manifest herself in them easier.<br /> <br /> As for summoning a whole Yozi, if I were to homebrew it you would need to prepare multiple rituals to summon every second and third circle soul at once, which of course would need to happen on calibration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 03-27-2019, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T14:43:30-07:00","id":1300390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300221#post1300221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Errrr, all of them. They're having a party; Sacheverell is passed out on the couch.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the fae start a-fallin',<br /> There's a gal you should be callin':<br /> That's E-M-P-R-E-S-S<br /> Let it ring!<br /> Solar Plow is a loser<br /> And I think he's a boozer.<br /> So you better make that call to Her Redness!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T15:51:11-07:00","id":1300405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300378#post1300378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was referring to summoning her Fetich Soul. Due to some rather strange aspects of her existence, she is much closer to her souls than the other Yozi, and can manifest herself in them easier.<br /> <br /> As for summoning a whole Yozi, if I were to homebrew it you would need to prepare multiple rituals to summon every second and third circle soul at once, which of course would need to happen on calibration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T18:46:53-07:00","id":1300444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300349#post1300349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why humans were not Geased - they weren't created by the Primordials</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I feel as though that gives the mythology a bit less heft then the idea that they could have been geased, but were overlooked because they were underestimated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T19:29:52-07:00","id":1300450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300233#post1300233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I'm planning on having her be an ally to the characters, and the easiest way I can think of to both have her care about them and to have them be able to relate to her is to have it so she created humans and based their minds and personalities on herself, thus providing a reason to care (she cares about her creations) and making her more sympathetic (since she based human minds off of her own, she is the most easily understood Primordial and the most human-like in mindset, and so is easier to empathize with).</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels...off. Primordials just aren't relatable like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T22:07:51-07:00","id":1300470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300450#post1300450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That feels...off. Primordials just aren't relatable like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Which is why I made a new one that is, and gave the explanation that the reason is because she made humanity.<br /> <br /> I also tend to try and make everything at least somewhat relatable, as I find it more enjoyable that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T06:51:50-07:00","id":1300537,"title":"","content":"Making a new primordial just so you can make it do something that subverts what a primordial is doesn't make you not subvert what primordials are.<br /> But it's okay, there's not much else to say and you are already set in your ways. Wish you luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T15:40:47-07:00","id":1300690,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12947_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12947\" data-vbnamecard=\"12947\">Enderdragon1201</a>, do you mind if some of the thread's discussion goes to other people's ideas about the prehistoric status of humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T15:59:35-07:00","id":1300694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300690#post1300690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, do you mind if some of the thread's discussion goes to other people's ideas about the prehistoric status of humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine by me, I'm also interested in ideas like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T18:58:28-07:00","id":1300724,"title":"","content":"Recently, I've revised some of my ideas about prehistoric humans re: prayer.<br /> <br /> Not with the idea that it was their intended function from the Primordials, I'm still iffy about that.<br /> <br /> But as a thing that could actually make humans worthwhile as slaves to beings that already have pervasive supernatural powers and (in at least the case of the Lintha) some form of automated labour. Humanity becomes worth enslaving because they're intelligent enough to meaningfully pray, and weak enough to bent towards that purpose, all in a manner the enriches the civilizations harnessing them in that manner.<br /> <br /> In particular, that they didn't take some John Adams approach of &quot;just expose them to dangerous situations and let their worship emerge naturally from that&quot;; I'm picturing something more enterprising in which prayer was treated as a form of labour, for which huge numbers of people were herded together and put to work of engaging in proper ritual for hours at a time. Put them in shifts, and one's favoured gods can be getting prayer around the clock. In the case of the Dragon King and a few others, the rest of the time they're free to wander for their hunter-gathering, as their owners have little care or concern for how they live or die, so long as they properly gather together in the huge open temples built for the purpose when the call goes out (with those who fail to do so being prime candidates for sacrifice, as are those who collapse in exhaustion during their prayer shifts).<br /> <br /> It would be a picture that would include some compelling images of ways in which worship is treated as a form of labour that continue in parts of the world to this day (and which can have relevance as a connective element for some gods in actual gameplay who are taking increasing liberties), and to me would form a fun point of comparison between prehistoric humans of Creation and some archaeological/anthropological speculation on the origins of highly organised human communities in real life (to the effect that people started using ingenuity to construct big communal worship spaces, and as time went on they became such nuclei of activity that agriculture developed around accommodating the construction and regular worship schedules, which then evolved into the temples being consolidated centres of manufacture, storage and distribution, and ultimately administration).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:05:11-07:00","id":1302168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300213-who-made-humans-any-edition?p=1300349#post1300349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea for 3e: humans were an accident.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a variation of this which I used during 2nd edition.<br /> Humans were not envisioned as a singular race but are a catch-all term for the two part soul structure that was developed after the vivisection of the Clay Man. The Exalted of the Primordial War resembled a cross between extinct early human subspecies and more fantasy inspired demihumans with the idea that some of the war veterans may very well be the last of their kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:07:33-07:00","id":1302170,"title":"","content":"Do you mean you'd get stuff like Neanderthal Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:13:00-07:00","id":1302171,"title":"","content":"Precisely that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}